# Documents the real, currently-deployed kubernaut-family git-hook
# configuration (6 repos: kubernaut, kubernaut-operator, kubernaut-console,
# kubernaut-demo-scenarios, kubernaut-v1.5, kubernaut-v1.6) as a concrete
# worked example for ../generate-hooks.sh.
#
# The live kubernaut-family deployment predates this template system and
# runs under legacy filenames (post-checkout-cursor-mcp.sh,
# _restart-kubernaut-family-daemons.sh, etc. -- see docs/findings/2026-08.md
# 2026-08-13 and 2026-08-16 entries for that history), so this file is
# documentation of an equivalent config, not literally what's symlinked in
# ~/.hindsight/git-hooks/ today. Generating from this file into a fresh
# output dir produces functionally equivalent scripts under this template
# system's own naming convention (post-checkout-kubernaut-family-mcp.sh,
# etc.) -- useful for a *new* family, or for migrating this one later.
#
# DAEMON_LABELS deliberately does NOT include
# io.vectorize.cocoindex-code.kubernaut-family (DB-backed, no per-checkout
# staleness risk) or io.vectorize.serena-multiplex.kubernaut-family
# (stateless relay, no file-state cache of its own) -- see
# docs/findings/2026-08.md, 2026-08-16 entry, for why those two were
# deliberately dropped from the real restart path after causing a restart
# storm.
FAMILY_NAME="kubernaut-family"
DAEMON_LABELS="io.vectorize.serena.kubernaut-family io.vectorize.serena-project-server"
DEBOUNCE_SECONDS=30
